  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/sinanoran/pdfwright",
  "published": "2026-11-22T12:04:00.723Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.1.1: a line break or another control character in a string no longer makes a save throw. Every line break (\\n, \\r\\n, \\r, U+0085, U+000B, U+000C, U+001C to U+001E, U+2028, U+2029) is a hard line break inside the same block, everywhere text is laid out (canvas text included); other control characters are removed; a lone surrogate becomes U+FFFD; metadata, font family and language strings are trimmed and cleaned. Text without these characters is written as before.\n\n0.1.0, the first release: a PDF writer for reports. Blocks (Heading, Paragraph, Table, ItemList, Columns, Callout, Drawing, Image) flow and paginate; tables stream their rows and repeat the header; a drawing canvas and a text measurer serve charts; headers and footers know the page count; fonts are supplied by the caller and embedded as subsets; right-to-left and mixed-direction text, and Arabic, Hebrew, Devanagari, Bengali, Tamil and Thai shaping through HarfBuzz, are written in logical order so the text can be searched and copied; output is deterministic; SaveAsync can be cancelled; PdfImageOptions limits picture size (40 megapixels by default).\n\nKnown limitations (0.1.0 and 0.1.1): the language review of the test text was made by an AI agent, not by native speakers (Tamil, Bengali, Thai and Marathi least certain); the viewer check was PDFium renders, and Acrobat Reader and macOS Preview were not checked; the speed and memory targets are missed (a 1,000-row table: cold p50 2,095 ms, warm p50 347 ms, 188 MB allocated); CJK fonts with TrueType outlines are accepted but not tested, and fonts with CFF outlines (Noto Sans CJK, Source Han) come in 0.2.\n\nFull notes: https://github.com/sinanoran/pdfwright/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
